### 9. **Pipeline Flow & Error Handling**

File: `/home/serhii/.vadd/worktrees/70b74396-387d-4161-8a2a-5f0b63dc63be/7907a9ac-8195-4be4-b663-61c7859e7e58/backend/app/Services/AuditReport/AuditPipeline.php`

```php
public function run(AuditRequest $auditRequest): void
{
    try {
        // ... analysis stages ...

        $this->reportService->createAndDeliver($auditRequest, $payload, $scoreSet->scoringVersion);

        $auditRequest->appendPipelineLog('report', 'Report stored and sent');
    } catch (AuditNotAnalyzableException $e) {
        $auditRequest->appendPipelineLog('not_analyzable', $e->getMessage());
        $this->requestService->markNeedsFollowup($auditRequest, $e->getMessage());
    } finally {
        $this->cloner->cleanup($auditRequest->uuid);
    }
}
```

**Important:** The pipeline catches `AuditNotAnalyzableException` only. If `AuditMailer->send()` rethrows a render or send error, it propagates up and is NOT caught by the pipeline's exception handler. This would cause the entire pipeline to fail.

